window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-b9b242960e2269f3"]={"zh":"<p><a id=\"september-28october-2-2026\"></a></p> <h1 id=\"2026-9-28-10-2\">2026 年 9 月 28 日至 10 月 2 日</h1> <blockquote> <p>完整文档索引请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。在文档页面 URL 末尾添加 <code>.md</code>，即可获取 Markdown 版本。</p> </blockquote> <p><a href=\"#/article/a-135e664cbdfe4444?anchor=september-28october-2-2026\">返回“新功能”</a></p> <p><a id=\"choose-gpt-61-sol-for-complex-work\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"gpt-61-sol\">复杂任务可选择 GPT-6.1 Sol</h2> <p><a href=\"#/article/a-ae24d057324a4938?anchor=gpt-61-sol\">GPT-6.1 Sol</a> 的性能接近 Astra，成本低于 Astra。你可以将它用于代码、应用和文档相关的重复性长任务。具体能否使用取决于套餐、客户端和工作区设置。详情请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-04895d13e978a931?sectionMissing=codex-2026-09-29-gpt-61-sol\" title=\"旧来源章节未在本地快照中定位，打开该文章；可通过官方来源查看当前章节。\">发布公告</a>（官网章节，需联网） <a href=\"#/article/a-04895d13e978a931\">本地页面（官方来源暂不可用）</a>和<a href=\"#/article/a-24e0a6ab1e90e5b7\">定价</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"delegate-ongoing-work-to-your-dot\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"dotdots\">将持续工作委托给你的 Dot（Dots）</h2> <p><a href=\"#/article/a-1323ad8861010e1b\">Dots</a> 是 ChatGPT 中能够持续运行并承担长期职责的智能体。你可以给 dot 设定目标，例如准备会议简报或跟踪项目更新，并定义它可以自主执行哪些操作。它会在不同对话之间继续推进工作，使用已连接的应用、创建文件，也可以将任务委托给 ChatGPT Work 或 Codex。</p> <p>先创建一个 dot，为它命名并按自己的需要进行设置。它拥有独立的云端电脑和浏览器，可以把结果交给你检查；当某项决策需要你的判断时，也会通过受支持的联系方式联系你。你可以随时检查它的工作或给它新的指示。Dots 正在逐步推出。请查看<a href=\"#/article/a-1323ad8861010e1b?anchor=access\">可用性说明</a>，了解符合条件的套餐、地区和设置要求。</p> <p><a id=\"use-gpt-6-astra-ultrafast\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"gpt-6-astra-ultrafast\">使用 GPT-6 Astra Ultrafast</h2> <p><a href=\"#/article/a-55cdea3737e39583?anchor=ultrafast-mode\">Ultrafast 模式（超高速模式）</a>可在 Pro $500/月套餐以及符合条件的 Enterprise 和 Edu 套餐中用于 Codex 和 ChatGPT Work。Pro 套餐会使用订阅内含用量或可用积分。Enterprise 用量按工作区的积分协议或美元用量协议计费。</p> <p>Enterprise 默认不开放此功能；工作区所有者可以为指定用户或整个工作区启用。要求推理数据驻留在美国境外的工作区无法使用 Ultrafast。</p> <p><a id=\"prepare-reusable-codex-cloud-environments\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"codex-cloud\">准备可复用的 Codex Cloud 环境</h2> <p>描述你的开发环境，然后让 Codex 安装依赖、准备工具并测试工作流程。<a href=\"#/article/a-7ac5ae1c18e03bf1\">发布环境</a>，即可复用准备好的文件系统。每项新任务都会获得彼此隔离的工作区。是否可用取决于套餐和工作区设置。</p> <p><a id=\"scan-repositories-with-codex-security-cloud\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"codex-security-cloud\">使用 Codex Security Cloud 扫描代码仓库</h2> <p><a href=\"#/article/a-10cdc56de63926b8\">Codex Security Cloud（Codex 安全云）</a>目前以研究预览版形式在网页端和桌面应用中提供。在有访问权限的工作区中，安装此插件即可扫描已连接的 GitHub 代码仓库或监控新提交。在创建拉取请求草稿之前，请先检查发现的问题、验证证据和可用补丁。</p> <p><a id=\"continue-work-across-devices\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"work\">在不同设备间继续 Work</h2> <p>如果工作区启用了 Local computer access with Work Cloud（Work Cloud 本地电脑访问），你可以在桌面端启动新的 ChatGPT Work 任务，然后在网页端或移动端继续对话。任务可以使用已批准的文件和已连接电脑上的工具；需要在该电脑上执行的步骤必须保持电脑在线。现有任务会继续使用其原有模式。</p> <p>请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-2c7688c996bc9669?anchor=continue-work-across-devices\">跨设备使用 Work</a>和<a href=\"#/article/a-d50d47c21e8fd4ad\">管理员设置指南</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"work-together-in-chatgpt-space\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"chatgpt-space\">在 ChatGPT Space（协作空间）中协作</h2> <p>在功能已开放的情况下，<a href=\"#/article/a-9eaf251f273c9bc9\">ChatGPT Space</a>会将 Pages 和已保存文件集中到一起。你可以让 ChatGPT 起草或修改 Page，直接编辑 Page，并与协作者共享。你可以在 Page 中使用 <code>@ChatGPT</code> 或 <code>@dot</code> 请求帮助，也可以使用斜杠命令生成文本、图片和可视化内容。共享前请先检查可用权限。</p> <p>从 <a href=\"#/article/a-71293722d815f9b8\">Space 入门指南</a>开始，或了解如何<a href=\"#/article/a-418e376165928c0b\">协作编辑 Pages</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"set-up-shared-team-workflows\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_1\">设置团队共享工作流程</h2> <ul> <li><strong>ChatGPT in Slack 和 Microsoft Teams：</strong> 在获准的对话中使用已连接的工具请求工作区执行任务。工作区管理员可以<a href=\"#/article/a-6be952b78a5da779\">配置部署和访问权限</a>。</li> <li><strong>Team Tasks（团队任务）：</strong> 通过团队服务账户和获准的连接运行<a href=\"#/article/a-81de09346a07fee6\">定时或事件触发任务</a>，例如生成项目摘要。</li> <li><strong>工作区连接：</strong> 管理员可以为符合条件的团队<a href=\"#/article/a-d409bf3c6a23c7d1\">连接公司管理的账户</a>。每个连接都使用对应已连接账户的权限。</li> </ul> <p>具体可用功能和支持的控制方式取决于你的工作区和分阶段推出情况。</p> <p><a id=\"sign-in-to-apps-with-chatgpt\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"chatgpt\">使用 ChatGPT 登录应用</h2> <p><a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/siwc/quickstart.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Sign in with ChatGPT（使用 ChatGPT 登录）</a>可让用户登录你的应用；符合条件时，还能在应用中使用 ChatGPT 套餐执行 AI 请求。符合条件的 Plus 和 Pro 用户可以在参与的应用中使用其套餐额度。</p> <p>面向商业用途的登录功能正与部分合作伙伴进行有限试用。开源合作伙伴和部分指定的私营客户可使用 ChatGPT 套餐用量。可从<a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/siwc/token-sharing-open-source.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">开源集成指南</a>开始。</p> <p><a id=\"extend-your-plugins-interface\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"plugin\">扩展 Plugin 界面</h2> <p><a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/plugins/build/extensions.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Plugin Extensions（插件扩展）</a>让开发者可以为 ChatGPT 添加侧边栏应用、对话面板、文件查看器和编辑器以及表单。Composer 提及功能目前仅在桌面应用中可用；网页版的 Free 和 Go 扩展即将推出。</p> <p><a id=\"respond-to-mcp-events\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"mcp\">响应 MCP 事件</h2> <p><a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/plugins/build/mcp-events.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">MCP Events（MCP 事件）</a>允许用户要求 ChatGPT 监控服务器更新，并在收到符合条件的事件时采取行动。例如，用户可以要求它总结新消息或回复文档反馈。</p> <p>此集成需要 MCP 2.0。ChatGPT 支持从 MCP Events 草案规范接收 Webhook 推送；目前不支持轮询和流式传输。</p> <p><a id=\"customize-website-annotations\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_2\">自定义网站批注</h2> <p>使用 <a href=\"#/article/a-04a85e845544535d\">Annotations Extensibility（批注扩展）</a>，可选择用户在你的网站上能够选中的内容、附加相关上下文，并在将反馈发送给 ChatGPT 之前提供预览和修改控件。Browser Annotation API（浏览器批注 API）可在受支持版本的桌面应用内置浏览器中使用。</p>","en":"<h1 id=\"september-28october-2-2026\">September 28–October 2, 2026</h1> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <p><a href=\"#/article/a-135e664cbdfe4444?anchor=september-28october-2-2026\">Back to What's new</a></p> <h2 id=\"choose-gpt-61-sol-for-complex-work\">Choose GPT-6.1 Sol for complex work</h2> <p><a href=\"#/article/a-ae24d057324a4938?anchor=gpt-61-sol\">GPT-6.1 Sol</a> offers near-Astra performance at a lower cost than Astra. Consider it for repeated, long-running work across code, apps, and documents. Availability depends on your plan, client, and workspace settings. See the <a href=\"#/article/a-04895d13e978a931?sectionMissing=codex-2026-09-29-gpt-61-sol\" title=\"旧来源章节未在本地快照中定位，打开该文章；可通过官方来源查看当前章节。\">launch announcement</a> (official section, online) <a href=\"#/article/a-04895d13e978a931\">Local page (official source unavailable)</a> and <a href=\"#/article/a-24e0a6ab1e90e5b7\">pricing</a> for details.</p> <h2 id=\"delegate-ongoing-work-to-your-dot\">Delegate ongoing work to your dot</h2> <p><a href=\"#/article/a-1323ad8861010e1b\">Dots</a> are always-on agents that take on ongoing responsibility in ChatGPT. Give your dot a goal, such as preparing meeting briefs or tracking project updates, and define what it can do on its own. It keeps making progress between conversations, using connected apps, creating files, and delegating tasks to ChatGPT Work or Codex.</p> <p>Start with one dot, give it a name, and make it your own. Your dot has its own cloud computer and browser. It brings back results for your review and reaches out through supported contact methods when a decision needs your judgment. You can review its work or give it a new direction anytime. Dots are rolling out gradually. See <a href=\"#/article/a-1323ad8861010e1b?anchor=access\">availability</a> for eligible plans, regions, and setup requirements.</p> <h2 id=\"use-gpt-6-astra-ultrafast\">Use GPT-6 Astra Ultrafast</h2> <p><a href=\"#/article/a-55cdea3737e39583?anchor=ultrafast-mode\">Ultrafast mode</a> is available in Codex and ChatGPT Work on the Pro \\$500/month plan and eligible Enterprise and Edu plans. On Pro, it draws from included usage or available credits. Enterprise usage follows the workspace's credit-based or USD usage-based agreement.</p> <p>Enterprise access is off by default; workspace owners can enable it for selected users or the workspace. Ultrafast isn't available to workspaces that require inference residency outside the United States.</p> <h2 id=\"prepare-reusable-codex-cloud-environments\">Prepare reusable Codex Cloud environments</h2> <p>Describe your development setup and let Codex install dependencies, prepare tools, and test the workflow. <a href=\"#/article/a-7ac5ae1c18e03bf1\">Publish the environment</a> to reuse its prepared filesystem. Each new task gets its own isolated workspace. Access depends on your plan and workspace settings.</p> <h2 id=\"scan-repositories-with-codex-security-cloud\">Scan repositories with Codex Security Cloud</h2> <p><a href=\"#/article/a-10cdc56de63926b8\">Codex Security Cloud</a> is available in research preview on the web and in the desktop app. In a workspace with access, install the plugin to scan connected GitHub repositories or monitor new commits. Review findings, validation evidence, and available patches before creating a draft pull request.</p> <h2 id=\"continue-work-across-devices\">Continue Work across devices</h2> <p>When your workspace enables Local computer access with Work Cloud, start a new ChatGPT Work task on desktop and continue the conversation from web or mobile. Tasks can use approved files and tools on a connected computer; keep that computer online for steps that need it. Existing tasks keep their original mode.</p> <p>See <a href=\"#/article/a-2c7688c996bc9669?anchor=continue-work-across-devices\">Work across devices</a> and the <a href=\"#/article/a-d50d47c21e8fd4ad\">administrator setup guide</a>.</p> <h2 id=\"work-together-in-chatgpt-space\">Work together in ChatGPT Space</h2> <p>Where available, <a href=\"#/article/a-9eaf251f273c9bc9\">ChatGPT Space</a> brings Pages and saved files together. Ask ChatGPT to draft or revise a Page, edit it directly, and share it with collaborators. Use <code>@ChatGPT</code> or <code>@dot</code> to ask for help in a Page, or use slash commands to generate text, images, and visualizations. Review the available permissions before sharing.</p> <p>Start with the <a href=\"#/article/a-71293722d815f9b8\">Space getting-started guide</a> or learn how to <a href=\"#/article/a-418e376165928c0b\">work on Pages together</a>.</p> <h2 id=\"set-up-shared-team-workflows\">Set up shared team workflows</h2> <ul> <li><strong>ChatGPT in Slack and Microsoft Teams:</strong> Request work in approved conversations using your deployment's connected tools. Workspace admins can <a href=\"#/article/a-6be952b78a5da779\">configure deployments and access</a>.</li> <li><strong>Team Tasks:</strong> Run <a href=\"#/article/a-81de09346a07fee6\">scheduled or event-triggered work</a>, such as project digests, through a team's service account and approved connections.</li> <li><strong>Workspace connections:</strong> Admins can <a href=\"#/article/a-d409bf3c6a23c7d1\">connect company-managed accounts</a> for eligible teams and workflows. Each connection uses the connected account's permissions.</li> </ul> <p>Availability and supported controls depend on your workspace and rollout.</p> <h2 id=\"sign-in-to-apps-with-chatgpt\">Sign in to apps with ChatGPT</h2> <p><a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/siwc/quickstart.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Sign in with ChatGPT</a> lets users sign in to your app and, where eligible, use their ChatGPT plan for AI requests. Eligible Plus and Pro users can bring their plan usage to participating apps.</p> <p>Commercial sign-in is in a limited trial with selected partners. ChatGPT plan usage is available to open-source partners and selected private clients. Start with the <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/siwc/token-sharing-open-source.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">open-source integration</a>.</p> <h2 id=\"extend-your-plugins-interface\">Extend your plugin's interface</h2> <p><a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/plugins/build/extensions.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Plugin Extensions</a> let developers add sidebar apps, conversation panels, file viewers and editors, and forms to ChatGPT. Composer mentions are available only in the desktop app. Free and Go web extensions are coming soon.</p> <h2 id=\"respond-to-mcp-events\">Respond to MCP events</h2> <p><a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/plugins/build/mcp-events.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">MCP Events</a> lets users ask ChatGPT to monitor updates from your server and act when matching events arrive. For example, a user can ask ChatGPT to summarize new messages or respond to document feedback.</p> <p>This integration requires MCP 2.0. ChatGPT supports webhook delivery from the draft MCP Events specification; polling and streaming aren't supported.</p> <h2 id=\"customize-website-annotations\">Customize website annotations</h2> <p>Use <a href=\"#/article/a-04a85e845544535d\">Annotations Extensibility</a> to choose what people can select on your website, attach relevant context, and provide controls for previewing changes before sending feedback to ChatGPT. The Browser Annotation API is available in supported versions of the desktop app's built-in browser.</p>"};
